    "text": "The UP government’s One District, One Product (ODOP) Programme aims to improve development and production of indigenous and specialized products. Ghaziabad is identified as a hub for manufacturing of General Engineering Products. Many of these manufacturers are small and medium industries that need modernization, machinery and productivity enhancement. AKGEC in its endeavour to promote Industry Institute Interaction, has initiated the proposal and got approval from Department of MSME & Export Promotion for the establishment of Common Facility Center for General Engineering Industry under “One District One Product (ODOP)” scheme of Govt. of UP at AKGEC Campus,Ghaziabad To implement this scheme, “AKG Foundation for Innovation and Product Development” has been incorporated as a consortium of 22 Industries and Academia, including some of the prominent Industries of this region. This CFC to be established at Ajay Kumar Garg Engineering College will have a High End Engineering Product Development Facility for Local Industries including Modern Tool Room, Material Testing Lab, Research & Development Lab and Industry 4.0 Lab. The Foundation Stone Laying Ceremony (Shilanyas) of Common Facility Centre for General Engineering Industry of Ghaziabad, has been conducted today in online mode by Sh.Yogi Adityanath ji, Hon'ble Chief Minister of Uttar Pradesh, in the",
