    "text": "Ajay Kumar Garg Engineering College (AKGEC), Ghaziabad, through its Value Education Cell , successfully organised an AICTE-approved, Self-Funded 5-Day Universal Human Values Refresher Workshop (UHV-II Refresher) from 24–28 November 2025 . A total of 27 participants —26 from AKGEC and 1 from Arya College, Jaipur—enthusiastically took part in the workshop and successfully completed the program. Objectives and Focus The workshop was designed as a process-centric, outcome-based program with the following key objectives: To enable participants to understand the reality of human being, family, society, and nature/existence through the process of self-exploration . To emphasize the importance of meaningful participation at all four levels of living— Self, Family, Society, and Nature —for a harmonious way of life. To provide a platform for reflection, dialogue, and experiential learning that connects Universal Human Values with both personal and professional contexts. The sessions were structured to encourage deep inquiry, self-reflection, and collective exploration , ensuring that participants could internalize the principles of Universal Human Values in a practical and sustainable manner. Resource Persons The enriching and reflective sessions were facilitated by: Dr. Gopal Babu , Head, Value Education Cell, AKGEC Dr. Manishi Mishra , Member, Value Education Cell Both facilitators guided participants through a",
